#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Compile ipplan text files + the manifest into ipplan.db (gen-3).

The gen-2 ipplan2sqlite engine absorbed as modern python: the same
text grammar (#@ masters, network lines, #$ hosts with ;-separated
options), stdlib ipaddress instead of ipcalc, and the gen-3 manifest
and flow-pairing firewall build on top. Provision and puppet read
ONLY the database at runtime; svn (the deploy repo's vendored
snapshot until then) owns the sources and this compiler is the build
step - run by seed.sh today, by the svn pre-commit/post-commit
pipeline in production.

Inputs (an svn-tree root):
    allevents/colo/<site>/ipplan   one file per colo site
    <event>/core/ipplan            the event selected by currentevent
                                   (missing file = no event compiled -
                                   that IS the teardown mechanism)
    currentevent                   key=value: currentevent, apt_freeze,
                                   change_freeze
plus the manifest parts (manifest.yaml + appstore.yaml today): merged
at the top level, a key in two parts is a build error.

The emitted schema is prod's verbatim (gen-2 tables.py: shared node id
space, network/host integer+text ip forms, option/package double
truth, service/flow ids, node-id firewall_rule, the node_any /
active_switch / firewall_rule_ip_level views) so every old consumer
keeps working - hardened writer-side: foreign keys ON during build,
UNIQUE indexes that turn duplicate hosts/networks into build
failures, and additive meta rows (schema_version, tool_version,
svn_revision, build_time, current_event, apt_freeze, change_freeze).

Gen-3 grammar extensions (prod files are unaffected):
    gw=<ip> network option   overrides the computed gateway (the lab's
                             gateway is provision1 at .2, not .1)
    IPv6 master optional     a site with no IPV6-*-NET line gets NULL
                             ipv6 columns instead of derived garbage

Usage: ipplan2db --ipplan-root DIR --manifest FILE [--manifest FILE]
                 [--svn-revision REV] <ipplan.db>
"""

